.\" Manual page for docmost-cli-attachment(1)
.\" Source: SPECIFICATION.md section 4.6, src/docmost_cli/cli/attachment.py
.TH DOCMOST\-CLI\-ATTACHMENT 1 "2026\-03\-22" "docmost\-cli 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docmost\-cli\-attachment \- attachment operations for Docmost wiki
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docmost\-cli attachment search
.I query
.RB [ \-\-space
.IR slug ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B docmost\-cli attachment upload
.I page\-id
.B \-\-file
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands for working with file attachments in a Docmost wiki.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS search
Search for attachments by name or content.
.PP
.I query
is the search string.
.TP
.BI \-\-space " slug"
Restrict search to attachments in a specific space.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as a JSON array instead of a Rich table.
.PP
Table columns: id, fileName, type.
.SS upload
Upload a file (e.g. an image) and attach it to a page.
.PP
.I page\-id
is the UUID of the page to attach the file to.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path"
Path to the local file to upload.
.PP
Prints the new attachment ID to stdout and a confirmation message with the
page\-embeddable URL (\fI/api/files/{id}/{fileName}\fR) to stderr. Embed the
result in the page's Markdown, e.g.
.IR "![alt text](/api/files/<id>/<filename>)" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Search for attachments:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli attachment search "architecture diagram"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Search within a space:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli attachment search "logo" \-\-space design
.EE
.RE
.PP
Upload an image to a page:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli attachment upload 019e997e\-e14c\-7de7\-a35c\-15089aaa306f \\
    \-\-file ./diagram.png
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
See
.BR docmost\-cli (1).
